WEBVTT

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:08.860
I know this is sudden, but would you 
be willing to play us in two days' time?

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.490
A game against Ryoin?

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:18.000
The school we were supposed to play
in our morning game two days from now

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.500
contacted us to say they have to pull out
as they've picked up too many injuries.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.840
I don't expect you to say yes, 
but will you play us?

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:31.010
Sure.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.260
What?

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.490
What? Really?

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.700
You'll be playing our second string, though.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.140
I'd planned to give them 
the day off, anyway.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.200
Call this number later.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.270
Thank you.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.270
Let's go.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.960
<b>Ikuta Inn</b>

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:42.470
<b>8/14         Ryoin Game</b>

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:42.470
<b>Field 2                           10:00~</b>

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.790
And that's what happened...

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.470
I hope you're looking forward to playing them.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:46.370
Well done, Yoshida-sensei.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.980
Oh, uh...

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:49.730
Hilarious.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:54.750
<b>Episode 22 
Your Turf</b>

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.550
It's practically your fault 
that we're playing Ryoin.

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:57.240
Well, yeah. You should be grateful.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.240
I'm terrified.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.790
What's wrong with you guys?

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:02.490
Aren't you happy?

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:06.610
Second string or not, Ryoin have ruled
Kanagawa for fifteen years straight,

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.120
and we get to play them.

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:12.120
Steal all the techniques and 
knowledge you can from them.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:19.580
Put some energy into
your afternoon match, too.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.760
Yes, sir!

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.760
Jinko

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.760
Wakimachi

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:29.430
Mattsu!

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.600
What are you doing?

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.770
Player substitution: fly-half.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.250
Oharano in for Matsuo.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.530
Here's your jersey.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:52.290
I'm exhausted. Take it from here, Oharano.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.030
Okay.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:18.730
Jinko

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:18.730
Wakimachi

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.490
Dammit. We lost.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.740
You let a lot of guys
get past you today, Gion.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.500
Ah, Kasuga-senpai.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:38.290
I was terrible today. 
Do you know what I did—

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.440
Be polite!

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:42.260
<b>GRIND               GRIND
 GRIND                 GRIND</b>

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:42.260
Kasuga!

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:47.900
Why'd he hit me, too?

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:50.510
I can't believe you guys lost.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:53.290
We won our match this morning.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:55.760
That makes our record three wins, two losses.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.650
Senpai! Senpai! Senpai! Senpai!

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:58.650
Shut up.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.650
What did I do wrong today?

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.300
Everything!

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:09.850
<b>GRIND      GRIND
 GRIND        GRIND</b>

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:09.070
But you know, Kasuga, you do have to tell him.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:13.400
We're playing Ryoin the day after tomorrow.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:18.250
Since it's their second string, the Kirishima
brothers definitely won't be playing.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:22.620
But they'll all be guys who compete 
with those brothers day in, day out.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:28.880
Gion's not the only one. 
We all have to practice harder.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.210
Oof.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:34.330
For example, Gion... Hey, come here.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:35.770
Okay.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:39.650
Your tackles down low, 
where you go for their heels,

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:43.780
are amazing.<i> Really </i>amazing.
 For the most part.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.210
But your positioning is all wrong.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:47.280
My positioning?

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.030
Let's practice a little bit.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:54.560
My right shoulder and your right shoulder.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:59.190
Practice keeping them opposite each other.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:06.380
That's it.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:18.980
You've got no feel for this, Gion.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:22.620
When your opponent's right shoulder
and your right shoulder,

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:26.790
or his left shoulder and your left shoulder, 
are directly opposite each other,

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:28.680
that's the right position.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:34.080
For example, suppose you end up in 
a scrum with the ball in their possession.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.440
From the scrum, they first pass to their #10.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:57.430
<b>Scrum</b>

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.730
The ball will keep moving 
towards the outside,

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:44.810
so we want to stop it as soon as possible.

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:49.760
If the space marked by 
each position is like this,

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:56.320
then there's this space between 
the scrum and the opposing #10.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.940
And who's supposed to mark this space?

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.820
The flanker.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.690
<b>G</b>

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:09.970
So when you enter the space marked by 
our #10 without considering your positioning,

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:17.450
<b>Scrum</b>

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:12.870
they can run past you 
through this open space.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:17.450
That's called an inside break.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:17.450
<b>Inside Break</b>

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.870
Only our #15 is behind you, 
so that puts us in big trouble.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:22.210
<i>Big</i> trouble!

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:27.710
The line we have to guard is the line 
between our opponent's right shoulder

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.210
and our own right shoulders.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:39.350
<b>Scrum</b>

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:39.350
<b>G</b>

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:33.690
As long as you maintain this position,

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:37.360
whether he darts right or jinks left, 
we'll always keep up with the play.

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:39.350
I get it.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:45.360
In other words, you've gotta 
protect your own turf.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.610
Yes, sir.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:49.620
Instead of talking, let's give it a try.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.200
Hey.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:55.700
Come on out. Let's practice together, Ise.

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:58.810
Why are you hiding back there?

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.500
Are you interested in being a flanker?

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:03.210
Er, yeah.

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:06.210
Okay.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:08.710
Gion, you're first.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:14.090
I'll be on offense. Let's pretend 
the backs are lined up to my left.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:19.100
Keep your right shoulder level with mine.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:21.940
Always keep your body 
squared up against mine.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:24.100
Keep your body bent.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.990
The ball's coming out of a scrum.

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:28.940
Okay.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:30.070
Here.

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.610
All right!

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:38.790
You're standing in the wrong place.

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:39.720
Ise, you're next.

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:40.660
Y-Yes, sir!

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:01.520
Your body's not facing forward.

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:03.600
You're getting knocked down because

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.350
you're desperately trying to match 
my position with bad posture.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.350
Yes, sir!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.770
Gion, one more time.

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:13.280
Dammit.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.780
Watch my movements.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.460
You're not keeping up, and you're 
forgetting to keep your body bent.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:19.520
Yes, sir.

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:20.470
Ise.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:22.770
Thank you!

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:25.890
All wrong.

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.370
Come on, you turds.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:38.760
One more time.

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:44.140
No matter what, two days from now,

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.950
I'll drag the Kirishima brothers
onto the field.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.520
One more time!

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:51.980
Yes, sir!

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:55.420
Too weak! Ise, you're next!

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:56.100
Yes, sir!

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.740
That should do it.

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:03.260
Good work, guys.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:04.490
Yes, sir.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:07.780
Although, Kasuga ran twice 
as much as you guys.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.700
I'm not tired.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:13.000
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.980
Hey!

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:18.510
So you were practicing here.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:22.640
I thought you might be here,
 so I made rice balls.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.360
Mutsumi-san!

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:25.430
Mom!

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:26.810
Who are you calling "mom"?

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:32.840
They're so good!

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.550
I'm seriously happy.

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:37.090
You really understand us.

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:40.570
All our flankers were missing.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.340
What? Natsuki, do you want to be a flanker?

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:46.330
Yeah.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:50.580
Actually, I... I want to be a forward.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:53.190
I'm glad to hear that.

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:57.590
If you take over as a forward,
Kasuga or I can go back to being a center.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:00.340
Senpai, you were a back?

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.170
...sir?

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:07.100
Yeah, although he started 
playing as a forward this year.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:10.610
We were worried since we didn't 
have many third-year backs.

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:14.360
Yeah. Keep training our flankers, Kasuga.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:18.110
Kasuga?

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:22.460
Kasuga, did you get it?

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:23.160
What?

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:26.490
I put a heap of wasabi in one of them.

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:32.660
No wasabi in this one.

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:33.460
Liar.

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:38.150
It's got nothing to do with these rice balls,
 but... Hachi, I'm going to punch you later.

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:41.230
What? It was only a game.

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:42.050
Shut up.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:44.300
Just admit it already, Kasuga.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:47.520
There's no wasabi in this one.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:48.490
Yeah, yeah.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:52.020
<b>POW</b>

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.020
<b>It 
wasn't
 me!!</b>

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:55.020
<b>There's 
no rice...</b>

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:55.020
<b>Hachioji-san
 just made some</b>

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:55.020
<b>You'll have to 
wait until dinner</b>

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:55.020
<b>I'm going to 
kill Hachi</b>

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:58.400
<b>Ikuta Inn</b>

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:01.900
We lost again!

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:05.000
Kamo-senpai, what are you doing?

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.660
Nice, Hirota!

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:11.840
The backs lost the "Forwards 
vs. Backs Bathing Order...

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:14.540
Rock-Paper-Scissors Tournament" 
for the third time in a row.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:19.850
We're going to be bathing in 
that half-empty bath again.

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:20.190
<b>Come On In</b>

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:24.850
No! I want to bathe in clean bathwater
at least some of the time!

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:26.640
Kamo-senpai, you idiot!

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:29.750
I thought you were the best on the Jinko team!

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.060
Let's go, forwards.

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:35.370
Wait a minute...

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.860
O-Oharano.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:40.070
Seriously, I can't take it anymore.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:41.820
You can't take it anymore?

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:46.630
I actually want to bathe alone,

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:48.960
but I've been sucking it up and 
bathing with everyone else.

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.540
Everyone feels that way!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:55.530
Also, the weird way the upperclassmen 
romp around is really annoying,

00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:57.140
but I've been putting up with it.

00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:58.710
R-Really?

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:05.040
And the bath is always kind of 
dirty after the forwards get out.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:25.610
Grumble

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:06.720
"Kind of dirty"?

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:10.040
I feel like there's some kind of 
weird oil floating on the water.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:11.990
What's it supposed to be? Ramen?

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:17.420
The sinks are full of filth, and the soap 
is turning black. It's like charcoal.

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:16.730
Someone stop him!

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:21.620
I'm at my limit. Give me a break, please.
I want to transfer schools.

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:23.120
It's no use.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:25.610
The stress from losing so much
has driven him crazy.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:29.870
Dammit! I know we lost,
but let the backs bathe first!

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:30.970
Don't be ridiculous!

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:33.400
You knew what you were getting into 
when you accepted the challenge!

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:34.620
Sit down!

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:38.850
Now we're pissed, so all the forwards
are going to sit and wash off the sweat

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.690
in the bath until we count to one hundred!

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:42.380
A-Anything but that!

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:44.010
Captain.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:46.510
Please do something.

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:51.010
Let's go, forwards.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.770
Our captain abandoned us...

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:57.040
Just give up.

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:00.900
No one can get in the way
 of Sekki's love of baths.

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:05.430
Bathing first was such a fleeting dream...

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:08.180
I want to go home, I want to go home...

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:10.570
I want to go home, I want to 
go home, I want to go home.

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:17.460
Hey. Are you heading down to the bath?

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.460
K-Komori-san.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:25.590
I actually thought
I'd join you guys for once.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:26.460
What?!

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:27.590
Is that all right?

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.050
O-Of course.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:32.570
You're split into your positions, right?

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.370
Then, I'll join the backs.

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:36.680
We all bathe together.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.440
Captain?

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.190
Let me use the shower!

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:45.250
You're getting soap on me!

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.760
Help!

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:53.700
<b>Cramped</b>

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:50.880
Do you guys really cram in here every time?

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:51.820
Yes, sir.

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:00.960
Spacious baths are great.

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:03.030
I've had enough!

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:06.210
This isn't fair! Let us in the women's bath!

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:08.990
You idiot!

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:17.720
Are you serious?

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:20.230
She kicked me as hard as she could.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:21.730
Of course she did.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:25.730
Ume-chan's the strongest one on our team.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:49.550
Hey.

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:53.800
How long have you been playing rugby?

00:15:55.570 --> 00:15:58.560
Since fourth grade.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.420
Why did you start?

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:04.940
Because my brother did. I just followed him.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:12.650
How'd you choose your position?

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:18.280
It was decided for me at some point,
so I just kept playing it.

00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:21.460
What about you, Suwa-senpai?

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:24.040
You seem like the type who's more 
interested in reading than rugby.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:25.950
Shut up!

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:33.550
What?

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:36.800
S-Sorry.

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:41.310
I don't like it when people 
say things like that.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:43.730
Sorry.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:54.320
Guys like you who can just "do it" 
without trying very hard are lucky.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:55.950
What?

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:58.090
But I do work hard.

00:16:58.090 --> 00:17:01.460
Then, don't say you're playing 
fly-half just because!

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:06.350
And don't look so unmotivated 
when you're getting game time.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.460
You were involved in today's game 
and yesterday's game!

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:21.970
You don't understand how it feels
to barely make the cut.

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.070
No, I don't.

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:26.520
I'm not interested in how 
other people feel, anyway.

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:31.740
Your arrogance annoys the hell out of me!

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:34.490
What did <i>I </i>do to make you yell at me?

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:46.750
I...

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:50.750
Ever since I was born, I've had bad eyes.

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:54.330
I hated how I was skinny and pale, too.

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:58.050
So I forced my way onto 
all kinds of sports teams.

00:17:58.690 --> 00:17:59.760
But...

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:06.490
But even though I train harder than 
anyone else, I never build any muscle.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:09.700
I don't get any stronger.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:12.150
No matter how much I eat, I don't gain weight.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.440
I never have any feel for the game.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:17.150
It gets to me.

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.650
The guys who don't try very hard.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.680
The guys who can casually do anything.

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:27.050
The guys whose hard work pays off.

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:32.130
I hate all of them.

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.670
Seriously, why was I...

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:44.060
Why was I born with this body?

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.500
Please stop!

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:56.000
Please stop.

00:18:56.890 --> 00:18:59.240
I really hate it when people do that.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:00.570
What?

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:06.990
Move over.

00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:08.710
Huh? Okay.

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:13.010
Senpai, do you watch professional rugby?

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:15.270
What? Yeah.

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:16.090
Here.

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:18.840
Watch red's #14.

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:20.610
#14?

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:23.600
He's the captain of
the Japanese national team.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:28.350
He's a really slow runner.

00:19:29.840 --> 00:19:33.630
Even though he plays wing
and captains the Japanese team.

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:36.910
There's nothing clever 
about his plays, either.

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:38.110
He's always covered in mud.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:40.610
He always gets involved in rucks, too.

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:43.830
It's like he doesn't care what 
a wing is supposed to do,

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:46.680
so he just does whatever he can.

00:19:49.190 --> 00:19:52.620
Why don't you try being like him?

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:56.050
What does it matter what 
your teammates are like?

00:19:58.410 --> 00:20:01.620
Just because they've advanced 100 meters,

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:06.140
is there any point in forcing yourself
to go 100 meters, too?

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:10.100
If 80 meters is the best you can manage,
isn't that good enough?

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:16.150
Advancing 20 meters more won't change much.

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:20.400
Guys who have advanced 200 meters
would never understand.

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:23.910
I'm not that far ahead.

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:28.410
Oh, wow.

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:31.410
That looks painful.

00:20:34.070 --> 00:20:36.420
The things you said earlier...

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:40.150
They're all things my brother said to me.

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:45.630
You're lucky, Ecchan.
You can do anything without trying.

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:49.370
I can't do anything even if I try really hard.

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:57.280
"Even though we're brothers, 
why was I the only one born this way?"

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:02.060
From my perspective,
my brother seems to be having more fun.

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:05.530
He has ten times as many friends as I do.

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:11.660
You got a photo of him?

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:12.350
What?

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:14.080
Of your brother.

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:18.540
I do, but say anything weird,
and I'll kill you.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:25.730
Your eyes are kinda similar.

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:28.030
Oh, really? Our eyes look alike?

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:40.820
Are you going back to your room?

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.190
I'm going for a run.

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:45.960
80 meters isn't enough to satisfy me.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:50.700
<b>Ikuta Inn</b>

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:48.310
See you later.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
<b>Next Time: "My Friend Taught Me"</b>

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:48.680
Next time: "My Friend Taught Me."
